{"name":"Custard Cream","hex":"#fbefd0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"custard cream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biscuit consisting of a soft, custard-flavoured layer sandwiched between two crisp biscuits."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custard_cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Custard cream","blocks":[{"text":"A custard cream is a type of sandwich biscuit popular in the United Kingdom, Ireland and parts of the Commonwealth. It consists of two embossed biscuits filled with a sweet, custard-flavoured cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/CustardCreamCookies.jpg/330px-CustardCreamCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Custard_cream"},{"title":"Custard","blocks":[{"text":"Custard is a variety of culinary preparations based on sweetened milk, cheese, or cream cooked with egg or egg yolk to thicken it, and sometimes also flour, corn starch, or gelatin. Depending on the recipe, custard may vary in consistency from a thin pouring sauce to the thick pastry cream used to fill éclairs. The most common custards are used in custard desserts or dessert sauces and typically include sugar and vanilla; however, savory custards are also found, e.g., in quiche."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Custard.jpg/330px-Custard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Custard"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dessertcustard.jpg/500px-Dessertcustard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Dessertcustard.jpg/500px-Dessertcustard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A formal custard preparation, garnished with raspberries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADessertcustard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/500px-Pastry_cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/1280px-Pastry_cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pastry_cream.jpg/500px-Pastry_cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c